    "canonical_url": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/gta-6-will-certainly-want-to-check-out-this-1970-ford-only-one-ever-made-278803.html",
    "origin_publisher": "autoevolution",
    "published_at": "2026-11-22T16:19:04+00:00",
    "published_at_raw": "2026-11-22T16:19:04+0000",
    "publication_precision": "TIMESTAMP",
    "acquired_at": "2026-11-22T17:35:16.874954+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-22T17:35:16.874954+00:00",
    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Honda CRF1150L Africa Twin Enduro Sports Is a Tongue Twister, Weighs Less but Offers More\nGTA 6 Will Certainly Want To Check Out This 1970 Ford, Only One Ever Made\n32 photos\nPhoto: eBay seller txchopper67\nA 1970 Ford Ranchero is selling at auction on eBay, and if you’ve played GTA 6 , you have every reason to be excited about this pickup truck. The reason is as simple as it could be: this is the first car protagonist Jason owns in GTA 6, albeit under a different name for obvious licensing reasons.\nThe Vapid Ganado is Jason’s original ride, and as I told you a few days ago, it’s based on the 1970 Ranchero in almost every regard .\nThis Ranchero is more than just a source of inspiration for Rockstar. The owner claims it’s the only one ever made in this configuration, and they also included the Marti report to prove it.\nPhoto: eBay seller txchopper67 The Ranchero lineup for 1970 included the standard model, the 500, the GT, and the Squire.\nBuyers who were specifically interested in a luxurious pickup truck were recommended to order the Squire. Described as “the new ultimate in personal pickup luxury,” the Ranchero Squire sported a contoured woodtone side and tailgate panels, plush full-width seats, wall-to-wall carpeting, a woodtone panel under the instruments, and an electric clock.\nFord also offered a long list of options, such as the Rim-Blow sport steering wheel, the SelectShift Cruise-O-Matic transmission, an AM/FM stereo radio, hidden headlamps, and the famous SelectAire conditioner.\nAs for the engine lineup, the Ranchero series included a little something for everybody, beginning with a 250 six rated at 155 horsepower. The Squire received unrestricted access to the most powerful engines in the lineup, so if money wasn’t an issue, you could even order one of the two 429 engines.\nThe Thunder Jet produced 360 horsepower thanks to a four-barrel carburetor and a 10.5:1 compression ratio, while the Cobra benefited from a higher compression ratio - 11.3:1 - to produce no more, no less than 370 horsepower.\nPhoto: eBay seller txchopper67 This Ranchero isn’t necessarily as special as a 429-powered specimen, at least not from an engine perspective. It is fitted with a 302 and an automatic transmission, but the original owner also ordered several desirable options, including air conditioning.\nThe 302 engine is now fully functional, but worth knowing is that this Ranchero has already received a tune-up, so it’s almost in perfect shape. It’s unclear if the engine was rebuilt, but the 302 was added to the list of items that were repaired recently, so I would call the seller and ask for more details on this front.\nThe clock in the dash is no longer functional, and the cruise control system also requires some attention. You can tell this isn’t a spotless car by simply looking at it, as it suffers from surface rust and blemishes that require some attention if your objective is a specimen in tip-top shape to park in your collection.\nYou get the obvious package, including power steering and power brakes, and the owner says the truck will come with a new hard cover and a new vinyl side and rear graphics.\nThe air conditioning blows cold but needs an in-depth verification because it’s still not running completely correctly.\nPhoto: eBay seller txchopper67 Now, let’s get to the thing that makes this Ranchero truly special. The Marti report that the owner has already ordered for this Ranchero Squire reveals impressive numbers, and there’s a good chance that this is the number one selling point.\nOut of all 3,943 Rancher Squires produced for this model year, only 1,099 were fitted with a 302 V8 engine under the hood. This is already a low number, but the report doesn’t stop here. It’s getting a lot more interesting, as only 74 of all these trucks were painted Light Gold. Only 54 people ordered the Nugget Gold knitted vinyl bench seats, and - this is the part where the numbers are getting truly impressive - only 3 were equipped with evaporative emissions.\nTwo of these Rancheros got the Visibility Light Group, and just one - this one! - came with air conditioning.\nIf these numbers don’t convince you to buy this Ranchero, I don’t know what will, so this is now the right moment to talk money.\nPhoto: eBay seller txchopper67 The vehicle is selling at auction, but the bad news is that a reserve is also in place. With only 9 hours remaining until the auction comes to an end, the reserve is still in place, so there’s a good chance the Ranchero will remain where it is for a little longer.\nThe pickup truck could find a new home at the very last minute, if one of the 190 people who added it to their watchlists decide to submit an offer that can unlock the reserve. The top offer at the time of writing is $7,271, and I expect the reserve to be somewhere around $10K.\nThe vehicle is parked in El Paso, Texas, and it should be able to go anywhere on its wheels, considering its fantastic shape.\nVia // eBay\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nford ranchero Ford 1970 Ranchero GTA 6 WEEKEND\nAbout the author: Bogdan Popa\nBogdan keeps an eye on how technology is taking over the car world. His long-term goals are buying an 18-wheeler because he needs more space for his kid’s toys, and convincing Google and Apple that Android Auto and CarPlay deserve at least as much attention as their phones. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1963 Buick Found in a Barn in Nebraska Begs for Restoration—and It's Unexpectedly Complete",
